[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA + injection seam (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSession accessor module as the single source of truth, with an injectable storage backend so unit tests need no [39m
     [38;5;246mDOM. Smallest design meeting all your answers; events can be added later without breaking readers.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: observable store
     [38;5;246mSession module emits change events; tracking and future forms subscribe. Most decoupled, but builds an event system
[39m     [38;5;246mfor consumers that don't exist yet.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m A, plain
     [38;5;246mSession accessor module using sessionStorage directly, no injection. Slightly simpler code; unit tests then need a
[39m     [38;5;246mDOM/storage shim.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m C: explicit wiring
     [38;5;246mNo singleton at all; login returns the identity and each caller handles it. Most testable, but no shared accessor [39m
     [38;5;246macross the app.[39m
